{"type":"text","timestamp":1790897450340,"sessionID":"ses_f06329e3cffenOq47GeB7kbAoJ","part":{"id":"prt_0f9ce371e001ELSDc7nlPKiy25","messageID":"msg_0f9cdffb5001mnNG4b9MxTp605","sessionID":"ses_f06329e3cffenOq47GeB7kbAoJ","type":"text","text":"I have all the source I need. Analyzing the four claims:\n\n1. **visible_at_deadline** — `__contains__` returns `self.timer() < link.expires`; a strict less-than means at exactly the deadline (timer == expires) it returns False → **not visible**.\n2. **expired_read_removes_storage** — expired `__getitem__` calls `self.__missing__(key)`, which only raises `KeyError`; nothing is deleted from `__data` → **False**.\n3. **assignment_refreshes_deadline** — `__setitem__` reuses the existing link, unlinks it, sets `link.expires = time + self.__ttl`, and re-inserts it → **True**.\n4. **expire_reports_removed_pairs** — `expire()` collects `(curr.key, cache_getitem(self, curr.key))` into `expired` and returns it; the docstring confirms this → **True**.","time":{"start":1790897436446,"end":1790897450333}}}
