{"type":"text","timestamp":1790897458206,"sessionID":"ses_f06329e3cffenOq47GeB7kbAoJ","part":{"id":"prt_0f9ce77b00018WGHY4eEdomypa","messageID":"msg_0f9ce6d620017C0FhqBhHxxvfw","sessionID":"ses_f06329e3cffenOq47GeB7kbAoJ","type":"text","text":"Submitted the answer. Summary of the findings from `src/cachetools/__init__.py`:\n\n- **visible_at_deadline (False):** `TTLCache.__contains__` uses the strict comparison `self.timer() < link.expires`, so when the monotonic timer exactly equals the link's expiration time, membership returns False.\n- **expired_read_removes_storage (False):** An expired `__getitem__` just delegates to `self.__missing__(key)`, whose base implementation only raises `KeyError` — the value remains in the underlying `__data` until `expire()` or an explicit deletion.\n- **assignment_refreshes_deadline (True):** `__setitem__` retrieves the existing key's link, unlinks it, assigns `link.expires = time + self.__ttl`, and reinserts it at the front of the LRU list, refreshing the deadline.\n- **expire_reports_removed_pairs (True):** `expire()` is documented to \"return an iterable of the expired `(key, value)` pairs\" and implements this by appending `(curr.key, cache_getitem(self, curr.key))` to a list it returns.","time":{"start":1790897452976,"end":1790897458199}}}
